You should only expect to see the all 1's == high factor score, all
0's == low factor score, when the factor loadings matrix contains
mostly positive values. Otherwise, the opposite will be true, but
again it's easy just to flip the sign in your factor score estimates
to fix this. Cheers.

Phil

